Z||000007||BENGAL4||02-15-2000||08:31 AM||||Gokart, I would love to see a rematch of the 75 series. I was in high school then. I remember thinking we had it wrapped up in game 6, when Carbo tied it up, Geo Foster threw Doyle out at the plate and then Fisk won it on the HR in the 12th. What a game. <P>Monkey, the strike turned me and alot of Reds fans off too. We started going to games again, just last year. My kids love it. I don't understand the mentallity that actors can get 50M for a film, but an athlete is looked down upon if they make any money. Look at Griffey Jr. He took less than market value just to come home. The impact of that trade is already being felt in the Greater Cincinnati area. Ticket sales are skyrocketing and with that, people are going to spend money on hotels, shopping, restaurants etc. I want you and your wife and son to join my family at a game this year. We will have a blast.<P>Bill    ||||reg||10
Z||000008||ChadMan||02-15-2000||08:35 AM||||Hey Bengal4, what's the deal with the Reds' new ballpark?  Are they getting one, and if so, when?<P>The Bengals are getting a new stadium this year too, right?  (Now if only Mike Brown would sell the team, maybe they'd start winning again.)||||reg||5
Z||000009||BENGAL4||02-15-2000||09:07 AM||||ChadMan, The Reds stadium is going to be ready for the 2003 season. It will be placed between Riverfront Stadium and the Firststar Center. Paul Brown Stadium should be finished in August. The local news is saying they are behind schedule, but who believes everything they see or read. After the Bengals move out, they are going to take approx 14,000 seats out of left and center fields at Riverfront. The new Reds stadium is designed so a left handed hitter can put a HR right in the river. As for Mike Brown, I don't like what he does but I'm thankful that he didn't move the team to Baltimore. They offered him that deal before the Browns. If the Bengals would have moved, Cincinnati would never have the NFL here again. <P>Maybe we could get the SW - Central Ohio Forum members together and go to a Reds game this year? Anybody interested?<P>Bill||||reg||10
